## Purpose
- Define current frontend/auth integration contract.

## Source of truth
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/environments/environment.ts`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/proxy.conf.json`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/nginx.conf`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/app/core/auth/auth.service.ts`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/app/core/http/correlation-id.interceptor.ts`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/app/core/http/correlation-context.service.ts`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/app/core/http/session-id.interceptor.ts`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/app/core/http/session-context.service.ts`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/src/app/public/pages/*`

## Do
- Use `environment.apiUrl = '/api/auth/v0.0'` for auth calls.
- In Angular dev server, keep proxy `/api` -> `https://localhost:8080` (infrastructure nginx HTTPS).
- In docker, frontend nginx on port `4200` proxies `/api` -> `http://gw-nginx:80` (internal HTTP to infrastructure nginx).
- Keep `withCredentials: true` on login/refresh/logout to support refresh cookie flow.
- Send `rememberMe` in login payload to control persistent session.
- Keep session restore via `refresh()` on app start (`restoreSession()` logic).
- After successful register, auto-login via `/login` and redirect to `/app`.
- Treat auth response shape as source contract for UI state:
  - `accessToken`, `expiresInSeconds`, `user`.
- Set `X-Correlation-ID` on every outbound API request via `correlationIdInterceptor` (new UUID per request).
- Set `X-Session-ID` on every outbound API request via `sessionIdInterceptor` (one ID per visit in `sessionStorage`).
- Reuse one `X-Correlation-ID` for the full register flow (`POST /register` + auto `POST /login`) via `CorrelationContextService`.
- Register interceptors in `app.config.ts` with `provideHttpClient(withInterceptors([sessionIdInterceptor, correlationIdInterceptor]))`.
- Trace create-account in Grafana: `{service=~"gateway|auth", env="prod"} | json | CorrelationId="<uuid>" | RequestPath=~"/api/auth/(register|login)"`.
- Trace visit in Grafana: `{service="auth", env="prod"} | json | SessionId="<session-id>"`.

## Don't
- Do not call auth service directly on `http://localhost:5001` from frontend.
- Do not store refresh token in local storage/session storage.
- Do not add frontend assumptions about endpoints outside `/api/auth/*`.

## Checklist
- Frontend calls still align with auth endpoints (`register`, `login`, `refresh`, `logout`, `change-password`, `users`).
- Local dev proxy target points to infrastructure nginx HTTPS port `8080`.
- Docker web container serves HTTPS on host port `4200`.
- Credentials mode is enabled where cookie is required.
